; Peer-to-peer gossip with three roles, parameterized by topic. 
; A seeder goes stale or keeps gossiping, infecting a relay while persisting; 
; a relay goes stale or forwards to a sink; 
; a sink goes stale or rebroadcasts, re-seeding and re-creating a relay.
; The variable rules seeder(x)/relay(y)/sink(z) abbreviate the ground instances on topic.
; Expected: WORST_CASE(Non-AST,?). Class: Right-Ground, Non-overlapping, Tail-recursive.

(format PTRS)

(fun seeder 1) (fun relay 1) (fun sink 1) (fun topic 0) (fun stale 0)
(fun infect 2) (fun forward 1) (fun rebroadcast 2)

(prule (seeder x) ((stale :prob 1) ((infect (relay topic) (seeder topic)) :prob 2)))
(prule (relay y) ((stale :prob 1) ((forward (sink topic)) :prob 2)))
(prule (sink z) ((stale :prob 1) ((rebroadcast (seeder topic) (relay topic)) :prob 2)))
